Mandy owes $100. The amount of interest she has to pay after 3 months is calculated by the formula:

\[
\text{Interest} = 100 \times \frac{1}{12} \times (2 - \frac{1}{3}) = 100 \times \frac{1}{12} \times (2 - \frac{1}{3}) = 100 \times \frac{1}{12} \times (2 - \frac{1}{3}) = 100 \times \frac{1}{12} \times (2 - \frac{1}{3}) = 100 \times \frac{1}{12} \times (2 - \frac{1}{3}) = 100 \times \frac{1}{12}
